434	52,425,542,902	434. Corolla of a Pentstemon, laid open, showing the 4 perfect stamens and the fifth as a sterile naked filament.	A Pentstemon corolla slit and spread open: five flaring lobes above a narrow tube, with four stamens in pairs curving up inside and a fifth bare filament between them.
435	515,1470,665,1752 - 628,1500,668,1580	435. Stamens (with a piece of the corolla) of another Pentstemon, with the sterile filament bearded.	A strip of Pentstemon corolla tube with its stamens standing up inside, the middle sterile filament thickly bearded with hairs.
436-437-441-442	504,712,1622,1752 - 518,755,618,1200 - 515,1470,628,1752 - 628,1585,668,1752 - 920,1526,1142,1752 - 1214,1390,1366,1724	436. Piece of Purple Gerardia. 437. Corolla laid open, showing the 4 stamens in pairs. 441. Plant of Hedge-Hyssop. 442. Flower laid open; one pair of good stamens; one pair of sterile filaments.	At left, 436, a leafy branch of Purple Gerardia with open bell-shaped flowers and buds; at top centre, 437, its corolla laid open with four hairy stamens in pairs; at right, 441, a slender Hedge-Hyssop plant with narrow leaves; below it, 442, a flower laid open showing two stamens and two sterile filaments.
438	518,755,618,1184	438. Style and calyx of the same.	The pistil of the Gerardia: a very long, slender style rising from a small ovary seated in the five-pointed calyx.
439	920,1526,1142,1752	439. Part of a pod.	Part of a Gerardia pod cut open, showing a thick wall and the many small seeds packed close on the placenta inside.
440	1214,1390,1366,1724	440. Flower of Toadflax.	A Toadflax flower seen from the side: a two-lipped corolla closed at the mouth by a swollen palate, with a slender spur hanging below.
